From 6d2f6a007d71f5a49322bd73e223165d3989bcde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tron <tron@tsm-consultz.dev>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 02:26:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(finops-suite): correct relative script paths + remove
 dead Vault calls

- 32 files under html/finops-suite/ referenced tsm-runtime-lock.js,
  tsm-event-contract.js, and tsm-autonomy-layer.js via a relative path
  (./html/js/...) instead of an absolute one (/html/js/...). Since these
  pages are served one directory deep (e.g. /finops-suite/x.html), the
  relative path resolved to a nonexistent /finops-suite/html/js/... and
  404'd, which killed window.TSMEventBus and broke TSM-KERNEL init
  ('EventBus not found. Load core first.').

- finops-operations.html (Branch Operations): removed the dead Vault
  system-prompt lookup. getVaultPrompt() posted {key} to /api/chat, but
  that route only ever accepted {query,...} or {message,...} - there
  was never a server-side vault endpoint, in this file or any other
  file that used the same pattern. Every page load fired 7 guaranteed
  400s (one per AI context) and silently ran every AI panel with an
  empty system prompt. Replaced with static per-context prompts inline
  (no network round-trip needed for fixed instruction text).

Verified via headless Playwright against a live server instance:
before -> 3x 404 + EventBus error + 7x /api/chat 400 on load;
after -> zero app-caused console/network errors, load time 1.3s -> ~0.5s.

Note: the same relative-path bug also exists in ~30 html/construction-suite
files, left untouched here as out of scope for this sprint.
